    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-11-08T05:04:04+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-08T05:04:04+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-07T18:34:04Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-07T18:34:04Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system centred south of SA will continue to drift eastwards, while a weak low pressure system and trough in WA move east across the SA border. The high will drift southeast of Tasmania by Monday, while the trough and low drift eastwards across SA, clearing to the east late Tuesday. Another high will develop south of the state on Wednesday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW014" description="North East Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-11-08T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-09T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-07T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-08T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower west of Leigh Creek later tonight. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Leigh Creek later tonight. Winds easterly 35 to 50 km/h. Daytime maximum temperatures 25 to 37.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">High</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:00am to 5:00pm, UV Index predicted to reach 12 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-09T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-10T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-08T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-09T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. The chance of raised dust west of Leigh Creek in the morning and afternoon. Medium chance of showers. The chance of a thunderstorm. Winds east to northeasterly 30 to 45 km/h tending northwest to northeasterly in the middle of the day then tending east to northeasterly 25 to 35 km/h in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 11 and 24 with daytime temperatures reaching 29 to 41.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-10T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-11T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-09T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-10T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. The chance of a thunderstorm with little or no rainfall. Winds northwest to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h tending south to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 15 and 25 with daytime temperatures reaching 34 to 39.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-11T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-12T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-10T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-11T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">The chance of a thunderstorm north of Oodnadatta in the morning. Mostly sunny day. Winds southerly 25 to 35 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 13 and 25 with daytime temperatures reaching 29 to 36.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
